<title>FRANCE: CCF H1 profit rises 12.2 pct.</title>
<headline>CCF H1 profit rises 12.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to June 30, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable			    668.8  vs	  596.1</p>
<p>    Operating				   1,489.1  vs	1,312.5</p>
<p>    Net banking income			4,813.9  vs	4,512.8</p>
<p>    Operating costs			   3,324.8  vs	3,200.3</p>
<p>    Provisions				    449.1  vs	  378.0</p>
<p>    Share in affiliates' results	     27.1  vs	   39.6</p>
<p>    Exceptional charges			  17.5  vs	   26.5</p>
<p>    Depreciation on acquisition costs	58.5  vs	   56.4</p>
<p>    Cooke ratio				 11.9 pct  Not comparable</p>
<p>NOTE - Credit Commercial de France reported its 1996 first-half results in a statement. It said net attributable profit rose 12.2 percent and net banking income rose 6.7 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;The recovery in volumes in a context of lower interest rates allowing the banking and financial activities to resume a positive evolution despite a new fall in margins due to brisk competition,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>The average analysts' forecast was first-half net attributable profit of 699 million francs, with the lowest estimate at 630 million francs and the highest at 848 million.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
